      "writtenOn": "2023-02-08T19:08:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We discussed the cpp_std side effect yesterday and concluded that it\u0027s probably best / easiest just to add `cpp_std \u003d \u0027c++17\u0027` to the defaults here. This will effectively ensure that whenever there is a mismatch between host and target cpp versions, the lower one is picked (Chromium is transitioning from c++17 to c++20 as we speak). Once that transition has completed (and we theoretically do not encounter any more mismatches), we can raise the value to c++20.",
